<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver markets shut for local holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver markets shut for local holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's gold and silver markets were shut on Thursday for a local Hindu festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>They reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday silver fell by five rupees per kg while gold was steady in a narrow price band. There is a shortage of ready metal and traders, in view of the wedding season, said they expected prices to firm in the next few days.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22 265 9000</p>
